   "id": "e2ad2252-6e09-4cc4-805c-603c7f12fb57",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Dataset Description\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5ebf4811-8080-48d2-914f-161a2f003feb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Brief description of the dataset\n",
    "The Family Income and Expenditure Survey 2012 (FIES) is a nationwide survey conducted by the Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA) to collect data on income and expenditures of Filipino households. The data from this survey is used to assess the socio-economic conditions of families across 17 regions in the Philippines. The survey provides vital information that aids in the formulation of government policies, economic plans, and poverty alleviation programs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e8885717-0db4-4b70-964f-e8b34594650f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Collection process and implications\n",
    "The FIES 2012 used a two-phase collection process, gathering data in July 2012 for the first round and in January 2013 for the second round. The survey covered a national sample of around 50,000 households and was conducted via face-to-face interviews with household members. The survey focused on detailed questions about household income, sources of income, and various types of expenditures (e.g., food, housing, education).\n",
    "Implications of the data include its use in shaping national and regional development programs, economic forecasts, and understanding the cost of living across various demographics. Furthermore, it provides insights into income inequality and poverty levels across different regions and social classes."
    "The two-round collection method reduces seasonal biases but still requires careful consideration when analyzing changes in income or expenditure between rounds.\n",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "92a809fe-305f-48fe-a5f4-295cfc515f3a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Dataset Structure\n",
    "- **Rows**: Each row in the dataset represents a household.\n",
    "- **Columns**: Each column represents a specific variable, such as income, expenditures, or demographic details.\n",
    "- **Number of Observations (Rows)**: Approximately 50,000 households.\n",
    "- **Number of Variables (Columns)**: Over 190 variables, representing detailed household-level income, expenditures, and demographic data.\n",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "10b17756-d388-47ed-9b27-f4ccd057b54d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Dataset Variables\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Household Identifiers\n",
    "- **W_REGN**: Region where the household is located.\n",
    "- **W_HCN**: Household control number, unique to each household.\n",
    "- **URB**: Urban or rural location indicator (1 for Urban, 0 for Rural).\n",
    "- **PSU**: Primary sampling unit, a geographical identifier used for the sampling process.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Demographic Variables\n",
    "- **SEX**: Gender of the household head (1 for Male, 2 for Female).\n",
    "- **AGE**: Age of the household head in years.\n",
    "- **MS**: Marital status of the household head (1 for Single, 2 for Married, etc.).\n",
    "- **HGC**: Highest grade completed by the household head (categorical).\n",
    "- **MEMBERS**: Total number of family members in the household.\n",
    "- **AGELESS5**: Number of household members below 5 years old.\n",
    "- **AGE5_17**: Number of household members between 5 to 17 years old.\n",
    "- **EMPLOYED_PAY**: Number of household members employed for pay during the past six months.\n",
    "- **EMPLOYED_PROF**: Number of household members employed for profit during the past six months.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Income Variables\n",
    "- **WAGES**: Total salaries and wages from both agricultural and non-agricultural activities.\n",
    "- **AGRI_SAL**: Salaries and wages from agricultural employment (cash or in-kind).\n",
    "- **NONAGRI_SAL**: Salaries and wages from non-agricultural employment (cash or in-kind).\n",
    "- **NETSHARE**: Net share of crops, fruits, and vegetables produced, livestock and poultry raised, either sold or consumed.\n",
    "- **CASH_ABROAD**: Cash or gift received from abroad.\n",
    "- **CASH_DOMESTIC**: Cash or gift received from domestic sources.\n",
    "- **PENSION**: Pension, retirement benefits, or other social security benefits received by the family.\n",
    "- **RENTALS_REC**: Rentals received from non-agricultural land or property.\n",
    "- **INTEREST**: Interest received from bank deposits or loans.\n",
    "- **DIVIDENDS**: Dividends received from investments like stocks and bonds.\n",
    "- **OTHER_SOURCE**: Other sources of income, including royalties and income from family members below 10 years old.\n",
    "- **NET_RECEIPT**: Total net receipts from family sustenance activities.\n",
    "- **REGFT**: Total gifts received.\n",
    "- **EAINC**: Total income from entrepreneurial activities (e.g., farming, livestock, retail, transportation, etc.).\n",
    "- **TOINC**: Total household income, combining all income sources.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Expenditure Variables\n",
    "- **T_BREAD**: Total expenditure on bread and cereals.\n",
    "- **T_MEAT**: Total expenditure on meat.\n",
    "- **T_FISH**: Total expenditure on fish and seafood.\n",
    "- **T_MILK**: Total expenditure on milk, cheese, and eggs.\n",
    "- **T_OIL**: Total expenditure on oils and fats.\n",
    "- **T_FRUIT**: Total expenditure on fruits.\n",
    "- **T_VEG**: Total expenditure on vegetables.\n",
    "- **T_SUGAR**: Total expenditure on sugar, jams, honey, chocolate, and confectionery.\n",
    "- **T_FOOD_NEC**: Total expenditure on other food not elsewhere classified.\n",
    "- **T_COFFEE**: Total expenditure on coffee, cocoa, and tea.\n",
    "- **T_MINERAL**: Total expenditure on mineral water, soft drinks, and fruit/vegetable juices.\n",
    "- **T_ALCOHOL**: Total expenditure on alcoholic beverages.\n",
    "- **T_TOBACCO**: Total expenditure on tobacco.\n",
    "- **T_FOOD_HOME**: Total expenditure on food consumed at home.\n",
    "- **T_FOOD_OUTSIDE**: Total expenditure on food consumed outside the home (e.g., in restaurants).\n",
    "- **T_FOOD**: Total food expenditure, combining home and outside food expenses.\n",
    "- **T_CLOTH**: Total expenditure on clothing and footwear.\n",
    "- **T_FURNISHING**: Total expenditure on furnishings and household equipment.\n",
    "- **T_HEALTH**: Total expenditure on healthcare services, products, and medicines.\n",
    "- **T_HOUSING_WATER**: Total expenditure on housing, water, electricity, gas, and other fuels.\n",
    "- **T_TRANSPORT**: Total expenditure on transportation (includes vehicle purchase, maintenance, fuel, and travel).\n",
    "- **T_COMMUNICATION**: Total expenditure on communication (telephone, internet, etc.).\n",
    "- **T_RECREATION**: Total expenditure on recreation (games, hobbies, books, newspapers, etc.).\n",
    "- **T_EDUCATION**: Total expenditure on education (tuition, school supplies, allowances for students).\n",
    "- **T_MISCELLANEOUS**: Total expenditure on miscellaneous goods and services (hairdressing, beauty products, etc.).\n",
    "- **T_OTHER_EXPENDITURE**: Total expenditure on other non-classified items.\n",
    "- **T_NFOOD**: Total non-food expenditure.\n",
    "- **T_TOTEX**: Total household expenditure, combining food and non-food expenditures.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Housing Variables\n",
    "- **BLDG_TYPE**: Type of building for the house.\n",
    "- **ROOF**: Type of roofing used in the house.\n",
    "- **WALLS**: Type of walls in the house.\n",
    "- **TENURE**: Tenure status of the housing unit and lot (owned, rented, etc.).\n",
    "- **ELECTRIC**: Whether the household has access to electricity.\n",
    "- **WATER**: Main source of water supply for the household.\n",
    "- **TOILET**: Type of toilet facilities used by the household.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Assets and Appliances\n",
    "- **RADIO_QTY**: Number of radios owned by the household.\n",
    "- **TV_QTY**: Number of televisions owned by the household.\n",
    "- **REF_QTY**: Number of refrigerators/freezers owned.\n",
    "- **CAR_QTY**: Number of cars owned.\n",
    "- **CELLPHONE_QTY**: Number of cellphones owned.\n",
    "- **PC_QTY**: Number of personal computers owned.\n",
    "- **MOTORCYCLE_QTY**: Number of motorcycles owned.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
